    <string name="tutorial_page1_title">Main flow</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page1_body">This app helps you organize photos on your device in three steps.\n\n1. Import\nImport from the gallery or files into Unfiled. You can optionally compress and apply default tags.\n\n2. Tag / rename\nTag and rename images in the detail or list views (rename templates are available), then move them to Filed or Trash.\n\n3. Export ZIP by tag\nWhen ready, pack Filed images into ZIP files by tag and share them.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page2_title">Before you start</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page2_body">A few things to know first.\n\n1. On-device only\nThe app runs entirely on your device: it does not use the network or upload your photos.\n\n2. Copies, not originals\nImporting copies files into the app\'s private storage. It does not move or change originals in your gallery or file manager.\n\n3. Actions affect copies only\nOrganize, rename, and delete only affect those copies. Optional compression also applies only to the copies, to help control size.\n\n4. Statuses are not tags\nUnfiled, Filed, and Trash are statuses, not tags—don\'t confuse them with your custom tags.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page3_title">A few more tips</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page3_body">1. Three statuses\nThe list is split into Unfiled, Filed, and Trash.\n\n2. Shared filters\nFilter by file name, tags, capture date, or import date. The same filters are shared by the list and export screens.\n\n3. Three ways to tag\nTags can come from the tag library, tag templates, or free input (successful new tags are saved to the library).\n\n4. Exported files\nFinished ZIP files appear under Exported files, where you can reshare, rename, or delete them.\n\n5. Settings\nLanguage, page size, default tags, and more live in Settings. You can reopen this tutorial from there anytime.</string>
